course: dictionary
lesson: 1077
title: Words for ocean giants
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A bowhead is a kind of whale. The context tells you this: «Bowhead whales can smash through ice with their heads to make breathing holes.» Whales need air, so a whale under ice needs a hole to breathe through. The phrase «bowhead whale» also shows you that bowhead names the animal.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The bowhead whale can smash through ice about 60 cm thick with its head» tells you it is big and strong. The dictionary says it is large, dark and lives in the Arctic. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The large Arctic whale can smash through ice with its head." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Bowhead is a noun, the name of a thing. You can say a bowhead for one animal and bowheads for more than one. When you write about it, bowhead whale is the full name and is always clear.
fact: A bowhead is a large, dark whale that lives in the Arctic.
fact: «Bowhead» is a noun: a bowhead, bowheads, or bowhead whale.
fact: A bowhead has no teeth. It filters its food using baleen.
fact: Its blubber, the thick layer under its skin, can be up to about 50 cm thick.
fact: Some bowhead whales may live for over 200 years, so they are among the longest-living mammals.
exercise: «The bowhead whale can smash through ice about 60 cm thick with its head.» What does a bowhead use to make a hole in the ice? | Its teeth | Its fins | Its tail | *Its head
exercise: Where does a bowhead live? | *In icy Arctic seas | In rivers in Africa | On tall mountains | In hot desert sand
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence «Bowhead whales can smash through ice with their heads to make breathing holes.» that means the thick layer of fat under a whale's skin. | whales | heads | breathing | *blubber
test: A bowhead has no teeth. What does it use to filter its food? | Teeth | Harpoons | *Baleen | Blubber
test: «Bowhead whales may live for over two hundred years.» How long might one live? | *Over two hundred years | Fifty years | Ten years | One hundred years
exam: Which word is a noun for the animal in this sentence: «The ___ swam under the ice to breathe»? | Breathing | Swim | *Bowhead | Cold
